WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.600
Episode 9

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.600
Revolving Defense<i>!!</i>  Asteroid Belt<i>!!</i>

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.600
( Air date: Dec 01, 1974 )

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:40.180
Space Battleship

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:40.180
<i>YAMATO</i>

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:41.110
The space battleship Yamato,
which is hurrying to Iscandar...

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:44.880
...was besieged by the
Pluto frontline base of Gamilus...

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:47.760
{HANSYA}...and it nearly became a victim
of the Reflective Satellite Cannon.

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:52.840
But the Yamato's indomitable spirit for
completing its mission led to the destruction...

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:57.010
...of the Reflective Satellite Cannon,
and turned the situation around.

00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:00.760
{FUKAI}Despite heavy damage,
it destroyed the base.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.410
{SOSHITE}The Shultz Fleet,
which escaped from Pluto...

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:07.160
{SOSHITE}...knows that it can't return
to the planet Gamilus.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:11.410
{DESLER}Lord Desler ordered
them to fight and die.

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:17.460
{FUKAKU}Shultz is going to risk his life in a final
battle against the damaged Yamato...

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:19.340
{FUKAKU}...which is in
desperate need of repair.

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:27.400
Unidentified flying
object detected.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:30.670
Commander Shultz,
it's the Yamato.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:36.070
It's unmistakably the Yamato.

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:39.500
Commander.

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:45.850
All ships.  All ships,
the Yamato has been detected.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:49.680
We'll charge the Yamato.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.930
Bearing EK5 111.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:58.310
Break formation, and head for
the coordinates individually.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:17.110
Mr. Sanada, hurry the repairs.

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:18.000
Aye, sir.

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:21.750
Shima, maintain slow cruise.

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:24.970
Groups 1 and 2 will take
charge of the exterior.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.810
Groups 3 and 4 will take
charge of the interior.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:31.910
The damage is heavy, and the work
will be difficult, but do your best.

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:33.110
Aye, sir.

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:37.160
Mr. Sanada, will the Yamato
be alright in this condition ?

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:39.450
Don't worry too much.
I have a plan.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:43.200
I guess it's time to propose
my plan to the Captain.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.510
Captain, the repairs seem to be
taking longer than anticipated.

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:25.910
I've detected something.

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:28.000
It's a strong signal.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:34.690
Captain, could that be the Gamilus
fleet that escaped from Pluto ?

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:37.020
Mori, recall
the repair crews.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:38.160
Aye, sir.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.510
But why is
there only one ?

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:43.300
It's impossible.
There must be more somewhere.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:44.750
All hands,
emergency alert.

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:47.300
All hands, emergency alert.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:49.500
What's happening ?

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:53.180
Bearing F25 316,
distance 52000.

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:56.620
Speed is 0.5 space knots,
and approaching.

00:04:58.210 --> 00:04:59.470
Captain...

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:01.060
...please, avoid any combat.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:03.400
The damage is
greater than estimated.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.650
I'm worried about how a
battle would affect the damage.

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:12.290
Captain, there are multiple signals ahead
and high to starboard. It's the asteroid belt.

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:42.670
It must be the remnants
of the tenth planet.

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:44.660
What tenth planet ?

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:49.760
It's been said that there were ten planets in
the Solar System. That must be what's left.

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:52.920
Shima, enter the
asteroid belt.

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:54.500
Aye, sir.

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:11.660
The Yamato has
changed course.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:14.240
Say what ?

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:17.030
They must have spotted
us and are running away.

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:18.410
I won't let it do that.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:22.810
If we let it get away, we won't be
able to return to planet Gamilus.

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:27.820
Tell all ships to pursue the Yamato,
and force it into X24.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:49.200
There they are.
They're heading toward us.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:53.270
We can't fight
in this condition.

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:57.050
Shima, synchronize our
motion to the asteroid belt.

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:59.720
Aye, sir.
Turning off the main engine.

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:24.870
The Yamato has disappeared.

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:30.750
What ? They must've noticed us and may
be generating some kind of jamming.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:34.100
Gantz, activate the video panel,
and switch to standard radar.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:34.790
Aye, sir.

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:38.150
What are they, Gantz ?

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:42.900
Sir, that's the debris of a planet.
There's an asteroid belt there.

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:45.220
Dammit.

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:56.480
No, they disappeared from radar.

00:07:56.480 --> 00:07:58.960
That means we're in
their blind spot as well.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:01.120
Hurry the repair operations.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:09.310
Mr. Sanada, it's fresh tomato juice,
made in the Yamato's agro room.

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:12.380
What are you making ?

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:19.140
It's an idea I came up with.
 I'm going to propose this to the Captain.

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:23.910
Oh, wait.

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:30.750
Asteroid ship operation ?

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:32.030
What do you think ?

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:33.850
Alright, proceed.

00:08:33.850 --> 00:08:35.800
Aye, sir.
Thank you very much.

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:48.660
Commander...

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:53.520
...all reports show that the
Yamato disappeared around this point.

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:55.960
It didn't warp did it ?

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:58.050
Should I consult
with the main base ?

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:02.250
Yamato, where did you go ?

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:08.000
Vice President Hisu,
I'm reporting.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:10.890
What happened, Gantz ?

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:16.290
We lost the track of the Yamato.
Is there any sign of a warp ?

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:18.560
You lost it ?
Idiot.

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:22.220
There's no sign of a warp.
Snap out of it.

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:25.190
Hisu, what's the fuss ?

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:28.700
Lord Desler...

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:33.520
Ask Shultz if he wants me
to send the royal guard ?

00:09:38.770 --> 00:09:40.140
Royal guard ?

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:44.430
Commander, could we be...

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:48.660
Find it !  Find the Yamato,
no matter what !

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:50.550
Don't overlook even the
tiniest piece of rock !

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:01.410
We'll begin the
asteroid ship operation.

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:05.520
If we succeed, we can
repair the ship safely.

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:07.560
Mr. Sanada, you lead the staff.

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:08.760
Aye, sir.

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:12.720
Kodai, prepare to launch
the anti-gravity inducer.

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:13.800
Roger.

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:18.250
Ready to launch.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:22.050
Angle is 40 degrees high
and low, and launch.

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:23.160
Launch.

00:10:55.660 --> 00:10:59.500
Disappeared without warping...

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:02.240
Asteroid belt, huh ?

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:05.950
I see. I got it.

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:10.960
The Yamato must be hiding inside there.
No wonder the radar doesn't work.

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:17.100
Gantz, tell all ships to investigate it
thoroughly, including every side of each rock.

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:25.600
Good.
That should be enough.

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:30.310
Repair crews, get ready.
I'm going to draw the debris closer.

00:11:30.310 --> 00:11:33.010
As soon as the debris is attached,
resume repair operations.

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:38.580
Attach the debris.

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:39.560
Attaching the debris.

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:15.890
Debris, attached.

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:19.050
Alright, Mr. Sanada,
resume repair operations.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.670
This is good. I feel great.

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:41.030
If you're born a man, you've
gotta drink in space like this.

00:13:41.030 --> 00:13:43.940
Oh well,
it can't be helped.

00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:50.940
Doctor, please be careful.

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:56.750
Shut up, Analyzer !
You don't have any sense of style !

00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:57.950
Oh, boy...

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:04.410
Yamato, identified !

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:05.760
It's there !

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:11.120
Where is it, Gantz ?

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:14.490
Where is the Yamato ?

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:17.820
Sir, I'm sure
I saw it, but...

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:22.850
Yamato, identified.

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:26.700
Which one is the Yamato ?

00:14:27.100 --> 00:14:28.060
Well, but...

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:30.110
Confirm its position.

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:43.010
Gantz.

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:46.310
Gantz, what're you doing ?
There's the Yamato.

00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:47.200
Oh, yes.

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:51.790
Tell all ships !
This is the final battle !

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:09.250
Yamato, I finally found you.
I'll show you what I can do.

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:27.050
It's quiet,
isn't it, Kodai ?

00:15:29.410 --> 00:15:31.660
How are the
repairs going ?

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:34.800
It seems that they're taking
longer on the third turret.

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:40.000
Everyone, how about some fresh
juice from the Yamato's hydroponics ?

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:42.260
Oh, thanks. {Thank you.}

00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:50.200
Tastes good.

00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:53.740
Indeed.  I'm relieved, too.
We all must be tired.

00:15:57.660 --> 00:15:59.060
Kodai, what's that ?

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:00.030
The Gamilus fleet !

00:16:01.630 --> 00:16:02.320
Enter.

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:05.720
Captain, the Gamilus
fleet is approaching.

00:16:05.720 --> 00:16:06.790
I know.

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:09.480
But what're we
going to do ?

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:11.700
Calm down, Kodai.

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:14.710
Stay alert, and continue
our repair operations.

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:21.690
This asteroid ship operation
is also useful for defense.

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:24.970
So let's try it
on this occasion.

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:45.110
Captain, we'll be in the
enemy's laser cannon range.

00:16:45.110 --> 00:16:47.200
Alright. All hands,
take your positions.

00:16:56.050 --> 00:16:59.160
That Yamato...
How pathetic it looks.

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:00.410
Commander Shultz...

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:04.310
...it must still be recovering from the
damage by the Reflective Satellite Cannon.

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:05.880
That explains its condition.

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:09.200
So the god of space is on
our side.  Commence attack !

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:20.230
W...what's the matter ?

00:17:32.510 --> 00:17:34.500
Dammit, we can't fight back.

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:43.800
Captain, there are
enemy ships behind us.

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:47.030
We have no choice.
Retrieve the repair crews.

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:51.460
Mr. Sanada, how much
longer can the debris hold ?

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:54.760
If we continue taking
a concentrated attack, it won't.

00:17:56.650 --> 00:17:59.160
Alright.
Revolve the debris.

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:00.190
Aye, sir.

00:18:00.920 --> 00:18:02.890
Kodai, connect the power.

00:18:04.820 --> 00:18:07.250
Activate the
anti-gravity inducer.

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:08.090
Activating.

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:13.660
Revolve the debris.

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:14.580
Revolving the debris.

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:41.170
What the...?

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:43.630
Commander...

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:44.970
Don't panic !

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:50.030
Our only destiny is either glory
or death. Only one of those two.

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:51.980
Fire !

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:54.090
Fire, fire, and keep firing !

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:14.340
The revolving defense of the
asteroid ring is a great success.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:18.870
This is a success ?
It's so frustrating.

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:23.270
Kodai, you know our defense
has to be complete also.

00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:25.810
Come to think of it, this is
the way the Yamato should be.

00:19:30.680 --> 00:19:34.690
Commander, the situation won't improve
at this rate. We have to do something.

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:40.630
Damn, I have no choice but
to take the final measure.

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:42.610
Gantz, crash into it.

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:49.520
They must be repairing the ship
while buying time like that.

00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:53.210
Once their repairs are complete,
they'll fire that Wave Motion gun.

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:55.410
Now is our only chance.

00:19:55.410 --> 00:20:01.770
If we can't return to Gamilus, we'll
sacrifice our lives to achieve glory.

00:20:01.770 --> 00:20:04.570
Commander Shultz.

00:20:04.570 --> 00:20:08.320
It's the fate of
Gamilus soldiers, so don't bother.

00:20:13.990 --> 00:20:17.160
Where you go, I go.

00:20:19.680 --> 00:20:24.340
All ships, we can't
let the Yamato escape !

00:20:24.650 --> 00:20:26.590
{SAIGO}We'll settle this battle.

00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:33.060
{SHOKUN}Everyone, it seemed long, yet it
was a short time commanding you.

00:20:33.060 --> 00:20:36.160
{KOREYORI}Now we'll crash
into the Yamato.

00:20:36.160 --> 00:20:38.060
{SORE}That's the only
option we have.

00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:41.160
{SHOKUN}Glory be to us all.

00:20:41.160 --> 00:20:45.940
{MEIOUSEI}To you brave soldiers of the Pluto
frontline base, just remember...

00:20:45.940 --> 00:20:50.700
{WARERA}...there are none braver,
before or after us.

00:20:56.120 --> 00:20:58.810
{SAA}Let's go !
All ships, charge !

00:21:15.320 --> 00:21:18.220
The enemy is closing in.
What're they going to do ?

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:20.770
Also from starboard !

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:22.170
From port, too !

00:21:28.540 --> 00:21:30.060
Stop the revolution
of the debris.

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:33.320
Shima, we'll lighten the load,
you evade their attack.

00:21:33.320 --> 00:21:34.090
Aye, sir.

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:04.600
It's no use, we can't evade !

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:08.700
Long live Lord Desler !

00:22:10.600 --> 00:22:12.700
Kodai, launch the rocket anchor !

00:22:14.360 --> 00:22:16.500
Aim at the belly
of that ship !

00:22:16.950 --> 00:22:17.990
Aye, sir !

00:22:18.540 --> 00:22:19.640
Launching rocket anchor !

00:23:11.300 --> 00:23:14.040
Shortly after, the repairs to
the Yamato were completed.

00:23:14.040 --> 00:23:21.090
The asteroid ship operation gave them another
hope in their journey of 296,000 light years.

00:23:21.090 --> 00:23:25.380
{CHIKYUU}The only things that can
save mankind from extinction are...

00:23:25.380 --> 00:23:29.640
{UCYUU}...love, wisdom, and the courage of
the space battleship Yamato's crew.

00:23:29.640 --> 00:23:31.910
Hurry, Yamato, before
our last day dawns.

00:23:30.500 --> 00:23:37.200
338 days left till the destruction of Earth

00:23:37.790 --> 00:23:42.550
Okita Juzo:

00:23:37.790 --> 00:23:42.550
Naya Goro

00:23:42.830 --> 00:23:48.060
Mori Yuki:

00:23:42.830 --> 00:23:48.060
Asagami Yoko

00:23:48.340 --> 00:23:53.560
Desler:

00:23:48.340 --> 00:23:53.560
Ibu Masayuki

00:23:56.330 --> 00:24:05.830
Note:
The Yamato launches the anti-gravity inducer from the secondary turret, but the barrels open wide horizontally.  Mecha illiteracy.

00:24:05.830 --> 00:24:15.830
Note:
The Yamato evades Shultz's kamikaze attack with the rocket anchor.  The anchor was launched from starboard, but the broken chain was attached to the port.  This was not only the animator's mistake, but also the director was to blame for overlooking it.

00:24:15.830 --> 00:24:25.830
Note:
Those episodes, done by Studio Mates, don't credit the chief animator,
but Mr. Kenzo Koizumi took charge of it.

00:24:25.830 --> 00:24:31.780
Note:
The Yamato took about 16 days to advance from Pluto to the asteroid belt, including the time for combat and repair.

00:24:32.360 --> 00:24:38.960
Translation

00:24:32.360 --> 00:24:38.960
Editing

00:24:38.960 --> 00:24:46.530
Timing

00:24:38.960 --> 00:24:46.530
Song Translations

00:24:46.530 --> 00:24:51.480
A
